WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.350
I won't...

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:05.940
...let you...

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.400
...pass me!

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.330
You're so strong, Mountain King.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.280
Your climbing strength is unbelievable.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.770
Your total control over your cadence,

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.160
and those eyes...

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.160
The large, honest eyes of a fighter.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.540
You've giving me goosebumps.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.030
<i>Be careful, Onoda.</i>

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.010
<i>Shinkai Yuto seems easygoing at first glance,</i>

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.640
<i>but he's fast.</i>

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.270
<i>And his movements are without 
mercy or hesitation.</i>

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.850
Yeah!

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.700
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.780
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.430
<i>LINE.11  Mountain King</i>

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:21.510
I was trying to surprise you.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:24.370
I'm even leaning against your shoulder.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.190
But that's odd.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.890
You won't budge.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.540
I'm going ahead of you.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.890
This is the power of the Mountain King.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.460
This is the Mountain King's turf.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.550
I thought you'd be blown away like earlier.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.010
I'm going ahead.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.180
You've gotten stronger in the past year.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.020
Far stronger than the rumors say.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.730
Yeah!

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.700
You're giving me chills.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.280
I get to race you, the Mountain King,
 at the Inter-High.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.180
You're incredible. Incredible.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.490
You're keeping up.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.910
I'm pedaling as hard as I can right now.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.040
Just kidding!

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.660
Shinkai-kun really is fast.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.000
He climbs like there's a 
motor attached to his bike.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.840
Yeah!

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.210
Try to keep up, Mountain King!

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:21.380
But...

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.410
I won't let him go. I won't let him go.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:27.430
Imaizumi-kun, Naruko-kun...

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.140
I won't let him go.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.280
I caught up!

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.870
You truly are interesting, Mountain King!

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:49.120
He accelerated again just when I caught up.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.010
<i>A man's spirit is broken when 
his opponent accelerates</i>

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.340
<i>over and over right before his eyes.</i>

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.290
<i>He believes his efforts will be 
wasted even if he tries again.</i>

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:03.110
<i>I'll keep pulling ahead of the Mountain King
 until his spirit is broken!</i>

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.260
<i>Over and over!</i>

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.610
Wow. You really are amazing.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.990
Your mental strength is incredible.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:25.190
That would have stopped an ordinary climber.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.910
But you're still following me even 
after I've pulled ahead four times.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.950
Exhausting yourself in the process.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.620
I'd like to know the secret 
behind your strength—

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:38.750
<i>Are you trying to pass me, 
Mountain King Onoda?</i>

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:39.970
It can't be.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:41.830
You're try to pass me?

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:42.720
Seriously?

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.200
<i>He's trying to get to the front.</i>

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.290
<i>Even though we're locked in battle.</i>

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:48.720
<i>Even though I've attacked numerous times.</i>

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:51.220
<i>Have I been beneath his 
consideration this whole time?</i>

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.730
<i>What is this, anyway?</i>

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.900
<i>His pedaling...</i>

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.090
<i>It's so plain and steady.</i>

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.180
<i>It's not special at all.</i>

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.840
<i>It doesn't even seem particularly fast.</i>

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.780
<i>But for some reason, I can't 
catch up to him easily.</i>

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.110
<i>It's like he's moving forward with certainty.</i>

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:09.030
<i>Step by step.</i>

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.990
<i>And with a strange rhythm.</i>

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.160
<i>I can't.</i>

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.460
<i>I need to take this seriously,</i>

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.920
<i>but for some reason I keep 
hearing the </i>Love Hime<i></i>

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.500
<i>season two opening theme inside my head.</i>

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.050
That's the secret behind the 
Mountain King's strength?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.740
Yeah!

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.140
I'm hurt.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.950
You passed me with such ordinary riding.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:39.520
I'm going all-out against you.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:43.030
You're plenty strong.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.280
I think you're amazing.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:50.950
But Teshima-san told me to reach the front.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.020
He told you to?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.620
How strange.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:59.070
Do you ride because you're told to?

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:00.960
Don't you not have a will of your own?

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.550
Are you a robot? A doll?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:09.170
I'm told what to do and do as I'm told.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.470
If that makes people happy...

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.520
Then that makes me happy, too.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.540
<i>Goosebumps...</i>

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.230
<i>These are different from the ones earlier.</i>

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.090
<i>Who is this guy?</i>

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.170
<i>I don't understand him.</i>

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:27.720
<i>I have to beat him.</i>

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.160
Can you hear the cheers of the fans?

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.490
The front is just ahead.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.000
Let's see who reaches the front first.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.210
It'll be our final race.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:43.920
Naruko!

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.900
What, hotshot?

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.380
They're coming from behind.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.880
I know.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.300
You're not going to check?

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.890
I don't need to look.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:56.010
It's Onoda-kun.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.410
I know this rising pressure.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:02.120
Onoda-kun is coming.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:03.040
But...

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:06.430
Feels like things didn't 
go quite according to plan.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:06.980
Yeah.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.860
There aren't many of them.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.620
Onoda-kun and one Hakone Academy rider.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:15.160
According to this morning's meeting, 
our strategy was to group up as a team.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:17.270
Did something happen?

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:24.640
So Teshima-san decided to send just 
Onoda after Hakone Academy attacked.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.000
Either way, we need to get ready.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.970
They could try to make a 
move once they're together.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:32.260
Things will change depending on
 who reaches the front first.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:36.600
And if Onoda's being pursued by 
that guy's younger brother, #16...

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:40.150
I know him well.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:42.600
After all, we fought one another 
at last year's Inter-High.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.770
He's strong and...

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:48.110
...obsessed with victory!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.310
Yeah!

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:59.160
Mountain King, I'm starting to understand 
how you won the final climb last year!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.210
Plain and steady.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.790
There's nothing flashy or cool about you.

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:04.760
Just plain, but with all your might.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.570
Steadily, steadily, steadily.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:07.670
You never stop.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.710
"You can't win like that."

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.800
"That's too plain to fight."

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.970
I'm sure you've heard that countless times.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:19.020
You suffered their criticisms and 
proved them wrong through brute force.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:19.910
Didn't you?

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.290
And so you ascended to your throne.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.080
You wanted to shut them up.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.360
Am I wrong?

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.650
It must've felt good.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.510
How was it?

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.910
How did it feel to prove everyone wrong?

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.440
To overthrow conventional wisdom?

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.650
Did it make you shake?

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:38.990
Did it give you pins and needles?

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:45.400
At last year's Inter-High, after the race,
 my hands went numb.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:47.880
My entire body was shaking from exhaustion.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.380
I'm sorry, though.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.180
There wasn't a single person 
 who said I couldn't win that way!

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:05.190
They were all so much nicer than I deserved.

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:09.820
My senior Makishima-san gave 
me a lot of encouragement.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.570
My classmate Imaizumi-kun...

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.610
...said he believed in me!

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:22.150
Huh. I see.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:24.220
<i>Is he serious?</i>

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:28.750
<i>He rides for the team? For one jersey?</i>

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:30.790
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.980
<i>So these people really do exist.</i>

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:39.090
<i>What other people think 
doesn't affect how I ride.</i>

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:47.370
It seems our attitudes towards 
victory are fundamentally different.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.060
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:52.540
<i>I have to beat him.</i>

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:58.920
<i>In that case, shall I prove it to him?</i>

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>Shinkai-kun!</i>

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.120
<i>He moved ahead. He's fast.</i>

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:05.930
<i>He's standing. He's dancing.</i>

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.220
<i>He's accelerating.</i>

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.920
<i>I need to keep up.</i>

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:11.890
<i>Prove I can achieve an overwhelming victory</i>

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:15.090
<i>over the man who sits on the throne my way!</i>

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.130
Fall, Mountain King!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.360
He's fast!

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.890
Hakone Academy jumped ahead!

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:23.140
He's trying to get ahead and 
meet up with the front first!

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.910
<i>He got so far ahead before 
I could even start dancing!</i>

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.560
<i>Let me catch up!</i>

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.930
If Hakone Academy catches up to 
the front, it'll be two on two!

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:35.440
The power balance will be a draw!

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.690
Either could attack at any time!

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:38.920
<i>I'll prove it...</i>

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:43.740
<i>By defeating the enemies behind me!</i>

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.750
<i>I'll prove it by pulling ahead!</i>

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.730
<i>That's my...</i>

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:50.750
This is Yuto.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.210
He's my younger brother.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.810
He started biking, too.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:55.820
Be nice to him.

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:58.340
Honestly, he's got talent.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.590
<i>Talent?</i>

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:02.140
<i>This is...</i>

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:05.260
<i>Shinkai Yuto's way!</i>

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.100
<i>Turn!</i>

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.310
<i>Catch up!</i>

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.300
Hakone Academy's faster!

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.400
Sohoku's #1 can't close the gap!

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.130
<i>Don't worry, he won't catch up!</i>

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:16.940
I...

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.610
<i>I'll get there first!</i>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.700
Yeah! First!

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:26.910
I'm here, Ashikiba-san!

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.920
Let's keep going.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:31.290
Let's leave Sohoku and 
their Mountain King behind.

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:34.000
<i>I beat the Mountain King!</i>

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.160
No. We shouldn't, Yuto.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.030
Why not?

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.780
The Mountain King is behind us.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:43.930
If grouping up was the battle, 
I beat the Mountain King.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.260
Sohoku...

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.140
Imaizumi and Naruko...

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.270
Matched Onoda's acceleration, 
and deliberately dropped back.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.800
They've already met up with him.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:58.230
You're always causing trouble, Onoda.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.100
Thanks.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.950
We've been waiting for you, Onoda-kun.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:07.200
If grouping up was the battle...

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:09.330
It's a draw, Yuto.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:13.570
I see.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:16.730
<i>I was going all out at the end.</i>

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:21.530
<i>I thought I'd pulled ahead 
and beaten the Mountain King.</i>

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:27.550
<i>I never thought Sohoku's riders 
in the front would fall back.</i>

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:30.310
They got us.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:35.310
If this were the finish line, I would've won.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.900
Team Sohoku...

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:42.440
...senses each other's vibrations 
and turns that into strength.

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:45.160
That's the kind of team they are.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.520
<i>Good. Onoda's here.</i>

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.370
<i>We have the strength of tag #1.</i>

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:52.120
<i>This will put a lot of 
pressure on Hakone Academy.</i>

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:55.990
<i>This climb will end soon,
 and we'll enter the downhill.</i>

00:12:55.990 --> 00:13:01.700
<i>For now, the battle for the second day's 
long climb to the pass is going well.</i>

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:04.000
How was Shinkai-san's little brother?

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.470
He was fast. It was like magic.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:12.390
Now we just have to wait for 
the other three to catch up.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.800
Um, well...

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:17.980
Imaizumi-kun...

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:19.750
Naruko-kun...

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:23.500
They're strong.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:27.040
If you say so, then they might be.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.570
Strong, huh?

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.080
Especially when they're together.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:33.120
Oh, that.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.410
You mean when their team is together?

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:38.170
In that case...

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:41.710
That might not be a problem.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.860
What?

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:45.610
Showoff and Aoyagi-san fell behind?

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:51.100
You're joking.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.020
Two of our six members?

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.140
It's still only the start of the second day!

00:13:56.590 --> 00:14:00.340
Aoyagi-san said he'd come back, but...

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:05.030
Teshima-san said we'd complete 
the rest of the race as four.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:09.700
Oh, right.

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:11.470
What about Kuroda-san?

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:15.280
He fell during the finish line 
sprint and started in the back.

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:18.110
Is Hakone Academy climbing as three?

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:20.130
That would mean they're missing one guy, too.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.350
Hakone Academy...

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:26.420
They dropped back together 
to collect Kuroda-san.

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:29.010
They're climbing with all their members!

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:36.020
<i>Who said we were doing well,
 Imaizumi Shunsuke?</i>

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.560
<i>This climb will end soon.</i>

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:43.190
<i>Are they trying to get here before it does?</i>

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:47.650
<i>Is Hakone Academy trying to gather 
all its members during this climb?</i>

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.660
Teshima-san will arrive before them.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.600
Once he's here, I'm sure...

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.120
And then the four of us...

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:56.610
If we accelerate, I'm sure—

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:57.620
Onoda...

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:02.160
Unfortunately, Hakone Academy
 made it here first.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:05.350
Looks like you're taking 
this seriously, Yuto.

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:08.630
Of course.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.100
Yuki-chan.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:13.530
I never thought I'd get 
to see you ride again.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.850
I... I...

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.590
What am I, dead?

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:18.350
It's not like I came back to life.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.940
But I thought...

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:22.820
Hey, you'd better not be crying.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:23.940
Teshima-san?

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:25.400
Hakone Academy...

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:30.360
Hakone Academy has gathered all its members!

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.080
Abs!

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.480
Lashes is shouting!

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:39.580
Where's Teshima-san?

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.080
Behind us!

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:43.470
Hakone Academy's passing us!

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:45.600
They changed formation!

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:46.670
This isn't good, hotshot!

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.960
They're making their move!

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:49.560
What should we do, hotshot?

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:53.010
Wait for Teshima-san, or chase 
after Hakone Academy as three?

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.140
If we let them go now, they'll...

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.650
Teshima-san, hurry!

00:15:57.650 --> 00:15:58.390
Hotshot!

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:01.070
<i>We don't have the numbers to go after them.</i>

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:03.210
<i>But if we miss this opportunity...</i>

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:04.980
<i>What should we do?</i>

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.570
<i>What should we do?</i>

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.090
<i>Teshima-san!</i>

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.360
We'll wait for Teshima-san!

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:16.200
Sohoku will accelerate once 
we have all our members!

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:21.000
Hakone Academy is accelerating 
with all their members!

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.590
They're getting farther and farther ahead!

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.590
We let them get away!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.950
Hotshot, should we send one of us after them?

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.340
Me or Onoda-kun?

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.720
We'll wait for Teshima-san! 
All of us, together!

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:33.400
<i>We'll wait.</i>

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.870
<i>That's right. I'm sure 
that's the right answer.</i>

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:37.930
<i>But...</i>

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:43.140
<i>It'll take just about 30 seconds or 
more for Teshima-san to catch up.</i>

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:49.100
<i>But staring at your opponents' butts while 
you wait makes it feel like an eternity.</i>

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:52.270
Hakone Academy is disappearing from sight...

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:54.090
Hotshot!

00:16:56.830 --> 00:17:00.900
Route 120, which connects 
Nikkou and Numata City,

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:05.040
switches from uphill to downhill 
at the Konsei Pass's Konsei Tunnel

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.840
1,842 meters above sea level,

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:09.630
where the course leaves 
Tochigi and enters Gunma.

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:15.550
Last year it was Mt. Fuji and Hakone.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:19.390
Why are road races held 
at the top of mountains?

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.720
I wish they'd hold one in the city.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.580
It's so hard to get around.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:26.310
I have to transfer trains and buses.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.270
The city?

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:30.440
Oh, not that I'm interested.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.760
I don't like city races.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.540
I'd be useless.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:39.780
Since that's what Sangaku said,
 I came all the way here.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.120
He's always late and never 
fills out his handouts.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.970
If he's not useful here,
 then he's banned from cycling.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:48.790
But...

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:53.250
<i>The view from the top of a 
mountain certainly is nice.</i>

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:54.340
They're here!

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:55.380
Huh? What?

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.270
Hakone Academy's in the front!

00:17:57.270 --> 00:17:59.650
Their second-year ace 
climber Manami is pulling!

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:01.930
And they have all their members!

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:05.780
They're here, they're here!

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:06.230
Wait...

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.940
He really is being useful!

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:11.650
<i>Last year, I couldn't give 
him those rice balls.</i>

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:13.820
<i>So this year, I know what to do!</i>

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:15.610
There!

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.780
I dropped all my stuff!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.640
<i>I don't have time to pick this up.</i>

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:25.080
<i>Since I came all the way here, 
I should at least say something.</i>

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.250
Sangaku, good...

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.160
<i>It's no use! I'm too late!</i>

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:33.920
Is this for me?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.760
Thanks, class rep.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:37.000
Huh?

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.550
Did you have a long trip?

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.580
Sangaku...

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.740
<i>I gave it to him...</i>

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:48.310
Go, Hakone Academy!

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:51.690
Teshima-san! Hurry!

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.860
<i>Come quickly, Teshima-san.</i>

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.820
<i>Hakone Academy is so far ahead.</i>

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.070
<i>Damn.</i>

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.230
<i>It's so long.</i>

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:01.720
<i>Does waiting always feel this long?</i>

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:02.910
I can't wait anymore!

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.120
Calm down, Naruko!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.620
We have to wait!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:09.460
A moment's decision determines 
everything in road racing.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:12.730
Will we or won't we respond 
to our opponents' movements?

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:14.170
That moment is now!

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:16.380
We have to go!

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.380
Even if it means leaving Teshima-san behind!

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.590
You must understand that!

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:26.190
Let's go, Onoda-kun.

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:27.620
Huh?

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:30.570
If we work together, we can 
still catch up to them!

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:32.120
No, Naruko!

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:34.440
Sohoku will accelerate once 
all four of us are together!

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:37.400
That's an order! Stop, Naruko!

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:39.450
Are you stupid, hotshot?

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:43.440
Whoever breaks the
 finish line tape first wins.

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.300
The favorites are riding in front of us.

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:48.780
Of course we have to go!

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.790
Hotshot...

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:54.500
I can't lose anymore.

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:02.580
Flashy when he wins, flashy when he falls.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:05.010
The fastest man from Naniwa. That's...

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:07.180
...who Naruko Shoukichi is.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:08.470
Naruko-kun...

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.050
Onoda-kun, you don't have to come.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.890
Damn it! He left!

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:21.340
Before he left, Naruko-kun said 
he'd defy your orders alone.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:23.030
That he wouldn't drag me into it.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.420
That showoff.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:27.740
You're self-centered, Naruko.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.620
Sohoku's #3 is here!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.290
Is he pursuing them alone?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.490
<i>Sorry, hotshot, Onoda-kun, and Teshima-san.</i>

00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:38.170
<i>But if someone doesn't go now, we might lose.</i>

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:42.050
<i>How could I not go?</i>

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.060
Okay, I've cleared the pass!

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:45.340
Now it's all downhill!

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.220
<i>I'll catch up to Hakone Academy!</i>

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.430
<i>It's one against six, but I'll show them.</i>

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.640
<i>Show them my determination!</i>

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.940
Nice timing, Naruko.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:01.170
Oh, Midousuji.

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:04.150
Are you going after Hakone Academy now, too?

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:09.270
You left at the very last 
second to catch up, Naruko.

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:12.160
As expected.

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:16.440
Hakone Academy would've sped up 
if I'd gone after them right away.

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:22.920
So I let them ride ahead, waiting until 
they relaxed and slowed down.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:25.880
And now you've started chasing them alone?

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:28.970
Oh, no.

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:32.770
You think I...

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:34.980
<i>Uh-oh, don't tell me...</i>

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:40.280
...would do something as reckless as Sohoku?

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:44.990
They're here right behind us.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:48.530
Komari-kun and my Zakus.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:50.530
All of them.

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:27.000
Manami-kun!

00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:29.300
You're as popular as ever, Manami-san.

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:32.350
Isn't Shinkai-kun cute, too?

00:23:32.350 --> 00:23:33.480
Yeah!

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:35.650
Shinkai-kun!

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:40.020
<i>NEXT LINE  Fallen Hopes</i>

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:45.020
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:51.250
<b>Don't miss the next episode</b>
